!slide Winner-Take All: An innocuous looking little statement

We find the following somewhere in virtually all attractor networks:

:: math
	\theta  \leftarrow \max_i { f(n_i, t) }\\
	\psi  \leftarrow  \arg\max_i { f(n_i, t) }

!when<1->
	and in an implementation of a WTA network, somewhere buried in our code, the
	math looks like this:

	:: python
		wp = G[:, t] + WP.dot(P[:, t])
		winner = np.argmax(wp)

!when<2->
	Two lines of math. Two lines of code.
